THE REGENT OF KLATEN

HAS DECIDED:

To enact : REGIONAL REGULATION ON EMPOWERMENT AND PROTECTION OF WOMEN.

Article 2

Empowerment and Protection of Women aims to:

a. increase women's participation in the development process;

b. improve the quality of life of women;

c. provide guarantees to women in the fulfillment of rights as human beings; and

d. provide a sense of security by increasing protection to women from various acts of violence.

Article 6

(1) Women have equal opportunities without discrimination to obtain employment.

(2) Employers who employ female workers are obliged to provide protection that includes welfare, safety and health.

(3) Protection as referred to in paragraph (2) is: a. health protection/insurance;

b. health services at the workplace;

c. opportunity and facilities to express breast milk or breastfeed at the workplace at designated times;

d. obtaining maternity leave for 3 (three) months after childbirth; and

e. obtaining balanced nutrition for pregnant women.

(4) Employers who are unable to provide protection as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be subject to administrative sanctions. Further provisions regarding administrative sanctions as referred to in paragraph (3) shall be regulated in a Regent Regulation.

3.2.text:
Article 12

The implementation of women's protection as referred to in Article 11 paragraph (1), may be carried out through efforts to:

a. provide and facilitate services for women victims of violence; b. Strengthening and developing service institutions for women victims of violence;
c. implement coordination of the implementation of policies, programs and activities for the protection of women among Regional Apparatus;
d. develop a data system for the protection of women; and e. conduct regional cooperation in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 10

The Regional Government is responsible for preventing acts of violence against women by way of:

a. Socializing laws and regulations;
b. Providing counseling/guidance;
c. Providing education on the dangers of domestic violence; d. Conducting seminars/workshops or the like;
e. Conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention; and f. Raising public awareness in behaving in accordance with religious norms and social norms.

